<section class="section" id="cost-comparison-aluminium-vs-tinplate-aerosol-cans">
  <h2>Cost Comparison: Aluminium vs Tinplate Aerosol Cans</h2>
  <p>Cost comparison must consider total landed cost, not just ex-factory can pricing. Raw material prices, energy consumption, transport weight, and minimum order quantities all influence final economics.</p>
                <p>In general, tinplate cans are cheaper per unit at high volumes, while aluminium cans carry higher material and processing costs but offer logistics savings due to lower weight. Can cost is only one line item in total filling economics — see our breakdown of <a href="/how-contract-aerosol-filling-works/">contract aerosol filling costs</a> for how component pricing fits into overall production cost.</p>

